# SonarQube (Cursor)

Vendored from [SonarSource/sonarqube-agent-plugins](https://github.com/SonarSource/sonarqube-agent-plugins) (SSAL-1.0).

## Setup (once per machine)

1. Install [SonarQube CLI](https://cli.sonarqube.com/) (`sonar` on PATH).
2. Authenticate: `sonar auth login` (token in OS keychain).
3. Run **`sonar-integrate`** skill (or `sonar integrate cursor --non-interactive` in this repo).
4. Enable **MCP → sonarqube** in Cursor Settings; Docker/Podman/Nerdctl must be running.
5. Optional: `sonar-project.properties` at repo root with `sonar.projectKey=...`.

## Skills (`.cursor/skills/sonar-*`)

| Skill | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `sonar-integrate` | Install CLI, auth, wire MCP + hooks |
| `sonar-list-projects` | List project keys |
| `sonar-list-issues` | Issues with filters |
| `sonar-fix-issue` | Fix one rule at file:line |
| `sonar-quality-gate` | Pass/fail + conditions |
| `sonar-analyze` | Analyze file/snippet |
| `sonar-coverage` | Coverage by file/line |
| `sonar-duplication` | Duplicated blocks |
| `sonar-dependency-risks` | SCA / vulnerable deps |

Invoke by name or natural language (“check quality gate”, “SonarQube issues on this PR”).

## Agent

**`sonarqube-reviewer`** (`.cursor/agents/sonarqube-reviewer.agent.md`) — read-only PR/diff review composing the skills above; does not edit code.

## MCP

Config: `.cursor/mcp.json` — runs `sonar run mcp`. Requires authenticated CLI + container runtime.
